{"kind":"promise","text":"I will repair the review basis for task/world-basis and re-request review on live bases only.\n\nBoth defects this request names are already repaired at head 51fb936e23b9e24ab59aee6df11d03a35389ba3e, each with a regression test: TestRetiringOnePredecessorDoesNotHideAnEarlierLiveOne pins that succession sees every earlier artifact at a path, so retiring the middle of A, B, C cannot hide a live A; TestArtifactCitingOnlyUnresolvableBasesCannotFlare pins that a statement whose every basis is unresolvable is marked unable to flare, with a resolvable-basis positive control so the assertion cannot pass for an implementation that marks everything. I will verify both under mutation rather than restate them, and carry them forward unchanged.\n\nWhat that head still gets wrong I will fix: OmittedSupersessions counts a live artifact as owing its retirement even when every later artifact at its path was itself withdrawn, so the page asks a reader to retire the current artifact for a replacement that no longer exists. I am filing that as a child request because it is beyond the two defects named here, and implementing it with a regression test carrying a live-successor positive control.\n\nI will then commit on task/world-basis with a Rests-On trailer naming this request, run make vet, make test, make race, make build and diff check, confirm a clean gofmt-clean worktree, and file a replacement artifact and a fresh exact-head review request to codex that rest only on live bases. This is a report of ready-for-review, not of completion; the merge is not mine to declare.","body":{"branch":"task/world-basis"}}